<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine's air force No.2 survives hijack crash.</title>
<headline>Ukraine's air force No.2 survives hijack crash.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The deputy commander of Ukraine's air force Viktor Strelnikov and two other Ukrainians survived the crash of a hijacked Ethiopian airliner in the Comoros, the foreign ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The ministry said the fate of a fourth Ukrainian on the plane was being checked. It condemned the hijacking as a &quot;shameful terrorist act&quot; and urged stronger international efforts to prevent such attacks.</p>
<p>The state news agency Ukrinform said the delegation had been in Addis Ababa for talks on modernising Ethiopian air force MiG-21s.</p>
</text>
